ormation Center, will close Colorado Highway 82 over Independence Pass between Aspen and Twin Lakes beginning at 8 a.m. on Saturday, October 31. The incoming storm is expected to bring snow accumulation and strong winds, making travel across the high-mountain pass hazardous. Conditions will be re-evaluated once the storms pass to determine whether the road can reopen for the fall or will enter its annual winter shutdown. CO 82 will be closed at approximately Lincoln Creek Road (Mile Point 51.1) on the west side and near Graham Gulch (MP 68.5) on the east side. The alternate route from the Denver Metro Area to Aspen is via westbound I-70 to Glenwood Springs, then CO 82 to Aspen.","impact":"minor","roads":"CO-82E","lat":39.120485,"lon":-106.686391,"chain_law":false,"closure":true,"pass_relevant":true,"observed":"2026-11-05T23:59:16.956Z","start_time":"2026-10-29T21:49:45.146Z","clear_time":null,"category":"Traffic","severity":"minor","source":"incident","geometry_kind":"point","distance_km":40.9},{"id":"OpenTMS-Event36252847861","title":"Hanging Lake Tunnel-152216","type":"Road Maintenance Operations","description":"Between Exit 129: Bair Ranch (6 miles west of the Dotsero area) and Exit 125: Hanging Lake (5 miles east of the No Name area) from Mile Point 126 to Mile Point 125. Right lane closed due to road maintenance operations. Starting Wednesday at 7:00AM MST until Wednesday, at about 7:00PM MST. Full schedule below: • November 11, 7:00AM - November 11, 7:00PM","impact":null,"roads":"I-70W","lat":39.586486,"lon":-107.19681,"chain_law":false,"closure":true,"pass_relevant":false,"observed":"2026-11-08T21:18:27.826Z","start_time":"2026-11-11T14:00:00Z","clear_time":"2026-11-12T02:00:00Z","category":"Construction","severity":null,"source":"planned","geometry_kind":"point","distance_km":69.3},{"id":"OpenTMS-Event36252847844","title":"Hanging Lake Tunnel-152215","type":"Road Maintenance Operations","description":"Between Exit 129: Bair Ranch (6 miles west of the Dotsero